      {
        "id": "E3",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "The AI Factory Operations Agent coordinates specialized sub-agents to detect failures, correlate root causes across compute, network, hardware, and scheduling layers, and surface recommendations through a chat interface for NVIDIA DGX SuperPOD operations.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/how-nvidia-uses-ai-agents-to-streamline-ai-factory-operations/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-04T22:00:17.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-05T02:20:16.822Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E4",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "The framework is built on the NVIDIA NemoClaw blueprint using NVIDIA OpenShell and runs fully on-premises with locally served NVIDIA Nemotron open models across NVIDIA DGX H100, NVIDIA DGX B200, and NVIDIA DGX GB300 production clusters.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/how-nvidia-uses-ai-agents-to-streamline-ai-factory-operations/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-04T22:00:17.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-05T02:20:16.822Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E5",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "For multi-tenant AI factories, scoped agents, tools, sandboxes, and Kubernetes permissions isolate tenant data and operations while central operations retain broader cluster visibility, enforced by OpenShell kernel-level sandbox restrictions.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/how-nvidia-uses-ai-agents-to-streamline-ai-factory-operations/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-04T22:00:17.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-05T02:20:16.822Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E6",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "NVIDIA developed the AI Factory Operations Agent to streamline its own internal NVIDIA DGX SuperPOD operations and reduce the manual effort by NVIDIA SREs.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/how-nvidia-uses-ai-agents-to-streamline-ai-factory-operations/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-04T22:00:17.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-05T02:20:16.822Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E7",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Instead of requiring SREs to check each layer of the AI factory software and hardware separately, the AI Factory Operations Agent uses specialized agents for different operational domains.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/how-nvidia-uses-ai-agents-to-streamline-ai-factory-operations/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-04T22:00:17.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-05T02:20:16.822Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E8",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "The AI Factory Operations Agent developer example was built around the NVIDIA NemoClaw blueprint.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/how-nvidia-uses-ai-agents-to-streamline-ai-factory-operations/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-04T22:00:17.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-05T02:20:16.822Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E9",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Agent inference uses locally served NVIDIA Nemotron open models, while the framework runs across internal NVIDIA DGX H100, NVIDIA DGX B200, and NVIDIA DGX GB300 production clusters.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/how-nvidia-uses-ai-agents-to-streamline-ai-factory-operations/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
